rom scratch  you can go to the cdc and who links in  this presentation for good information  about how to develop a protocol  thank you and thank you for our audience  member questions coming in  these are wonderful what is your  inspection control  does it not see benefit in screening for  cpo carriers  could you say that again please what if  your infection control does not see  benefit  in screening for cpo carriers  not saying benefit is a different issue  from not having the resources or the  institutional support for screening  if infection control does not see  benefit  there is a need for education cpas are  different from other gram-negative  pathogens  and the consequences of exit acquisition  can be very bad this needs to be  understood  educate about things like unacceptably  high mortality associated with cpo  infections  and the vital role of infection  prevention and control  cannot be over emphasized  cpos have become an international  priority with the who  proposing international regulations that  require countries to report events  of new or emerging antibiotic resistance  especially  cpos if you want to talk costs  cpas generate enormous costs associated  with not  detecting and not controlling spread  then there are costs to patients  what about the homeowner admitted to  hospital complaining of abdominal pain  and a lot of difficulty urinating  he gets a cpo infection and a few months  later the hospital owns his house and  he's leaving with his toe tagged  lots of reasons to screen for cpos  thank you for that our next question  coming in from an audience member  is how is waste water tested dr thompson  there's no standardized methodology for  testing wastewater  for getting samples some places  uh swab the surface of pipes  uh if you want to get the water you can  get it from a youtube under a sink  or open a manhole cover and drop a jar  in attached to a string  and collects a large volume of water  50 to 200 mils say maybe centrifuges  and